#: src/help.php
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Undergrowth reads your published posts and asks you about them. It never writes a word your readers will see, and it changes a post only when you accept a suggestion."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Your garden is every published post Undergrowth reads, without a password, except the posts you moved to compost."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Each suggestion is a link from one of your posts to another, at a sentence you wrote. The highlighted words are the words Accept will make into the link."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Choose words lets you pick other words of the same sentence for the link: choose the first word and the last, then save. Only words already in your sentence can be chosen; nothing can be typed or added."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Accept adds that one link and saves a revision, so you can see or undo the change. Veto removes the suggestion, and it is never suggested again, even after you edit either post. The notice after a veto has an Undo, in case you chose it by mistake."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "An orphan is a post in your garden that no accepted link from another of your published posts points to. Readers who follow links, and search engines, reach it less easily. Undergrowth only knows the links it suggested and you accepted, so a link you added by hand is not counted."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Beside each orphan are the best suggestions that would link to it, with Accept and Veto as on the Suggestions tab. Once you accept one, the post leaves the list. Composting posts and posts not read yet are never listed."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Seedling: a new post, with no more than one accepted link in or out."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Sprout: two or more accepted links, but not yet in a group of three or more posts on the Map."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Budding: in a group, with accepted links both in and out."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Evergreen: in a group, with three or more links in. In this version a post becomes evergreen only when you pin it there."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Stages are measured once a month from the links you have accepted, and never lowered. Pin a stage to keep a post at it, and unpin it to have it measured again."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Each group is a set of your posts that are close in meaning, found once a month. A group is named after the title of its post nearest the middle, with a few words its posts share that the rest of your site rarely uses. Every word is your own; nothing on the Map is written by a model."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "A post is not in a group yet when it has not been read, was read after the groups were last found, or is not close enough in meaning to two other posts. Composting posts rest outside the groups and are only counted."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "A group marked “with a gap” has no post at its middle: its posts circle something none of them is about yet. Whether to write about it is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "When a post you moved to compost sits near a group that is new this month, a notice says so here. Return it to the garden or dismiss the notice; either is fine."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Export, at the end of the Map, downloads every post on it as CSV for a spreadsheet or as a Markdown table for your notes: one row per post, with its group, the group's words, its link, its stage and whether its group has a gap."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Compost rests a post. It stays published, its links stay in place, and readers see no difference. Nothing is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "A composting post leaves the garden: no link is suggested to or from it, and its stage does not change. Undergrowth may still draw on it for a question to you."
msgstr ""

#: src/help.php
msgid "Return to garden brings it back, and its stage is measured again from the links you have accepted."
msgstr ""

